.TH FACEAUTH 1 "2026-11" "faceauth 0.10.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
faceauth \- manage face authentication
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B faceauth
.RB [ \-u
.IR user ]
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B faceauth
enrolls, tests, and removes face data and chooses which services use face
authentication. All work is done by
.BR faceauth-daemon (8)
over D-Bus. Commands that change data ask for your password through polkit;
in a terminal a text prompt is shown.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR add " [" \-c\ \fIcamera\fR ]
Capture a new enrollment batch of five face images from different angles.
On the first enrollment, choose the camera by index (2), device path
(/dev/video2), or udev name from /dev/v4l/by-id or /dev/v4l/by-path; without
.B \-c
you are prompted. Later enrollments reuse the enrolled camera.
.TP
.BR test " [" \-t\ \fIseconds\fR ]
Try to recognize you. Exit status 0 on success. Requires a local, foreground
session;
.I seconds
is capped at 30 (default:
.B timeout
from
.BR faceauth.conf (5)).
.TP
.BR clear " [" \-b\ \fIbatch\fR "] [" \-y ]
Delete all face data, or one enrollment batch. Asks for confirmation unless
.B \-y
is given.
.TP
.BR info " [" \-\-json ]
Show the enrolled camera and number of batches.
.TP
.BR cameras " [" \-\-json ]
List cameras. IR (greyscale-only) cameras are marked; they are much harder to
fool with a photo.
.TP
.BR "service list" " [" \-\-json ]
.TQ
.BI "service enable " name
.TQ
.BI "service disable " name
Show or change which PAM services use face authentication for you. Only
services listed by the administrator in
.BR faceauth.conf (5)
can be enabled.
.TP
.BR doctor " [" \-\-json ]
Check configuration, PAM wiring, cameras, the notification agent, the
daemon, your enrollment and services, and whether sudo authenticates root
(targetpw). Exit status 1 if a check fails.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-user " \fIuser\fR"
Operate on another account. Reading it
.RB ( info ", " "service list" ", " test )
requires root; changing it
.RB ( add ", " clear ", " "service enable" / disable )
requires administrator authorization (polkit
.BR manage-other ).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B FACEAUTH_BUS=session
Talk to a development daemon on the session bus
.RB ( "faceauth-daemon \-\-session-bus" ).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on failure, 2 on usage errors.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR faceauth.conf (5),
.BR faceauth-daemon (8),
.BR pam_faceauth (8)
